1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:02,240
Meet Veri Gate.

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:08,750
A practical way to record who is driving, which vehicle is moving, and when it passes through the gate.

3
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:11,314
Let's follow a typical movement.

4
00:00:12,155 --> 00:00:16,680
First, scan the driver's badge, or enter their employee number.

5
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:23,176
The screen brings up the driver and their authorization status, so the operator has the context they need.

6
00:00:23,988 --> 00:00:26,889
Next, scan the vehicle barcode.

7
00:00:26,839 --> 00:00:30,744
For a known vehicle, its details appear on screen.

8
00:00:30,744 --> 00:00:36,891
If it is new to inventory, Veri Gate adds a record automatically as the movement is processed.

9
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:41,619
Choose in or out, review the movement, and submit.

10
00:00:41,569 --> 00:00:46,904
The record includes the driver, vehicle, gate, device, and time.

11
00:00:46,904 --> 00:00:51,350
The scanner then returns to the start, ready for the next vehicle.

12
00:00:52,197 --> 00:00:56,103
A newly added vehicle can leave through the normal process.

13
00:00:56,053 --> 00:00:59,378
Missing inventory details do not hold it up.

14
00:00:59,378 --> 00:01:03,772
The usual driver authorization and license checks still apply.

15
00:01:04,613 --> 00:01:10,414
When a driver needs temporary authorization, a Fleet Lead or higher role can approve it.

16
00:01:10,364 --> 00:01:15,789
The prototype records that decision, keeping the exception connected to the movement.

17
00:01:16,613 --> 00:01:20,829
The desktop console brings the operational records together.

18
00:01:20,779 --> 00:01:27,931
Supervisors can manage drivers, update vehicle details, and review the devices assigned to each location.

19
00:01:28,738 --> 00:01:35,763
When a question comes up later, search the movement history by driver, vehicle, location, or date.

20
00:01:35,713 --> 00:01:39,192
The details captured at the gate are there to review.

21
00:01:40,030 --> 00:01:46,140
This review build runs on Android and stores records on the device, including without a signal.

22
00:01:46,090 --> 00:01:51,077
Shared cloud data and automatic synchronization are still being developed.

23
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:54,917
For now, it is ready to explore the gate workflow.

24
00:01:55,738 --> 00:01:57,492
Veri Gate.

25
00:01:57,442 --> 00:02:02,288
A focused workflow at the gate, and a clearer record to work from afterward.
